        composite:
          source:
            rid: 4065707203109847081
          reason: 1
          reasonNote: Hosts a whole Pyre layer and lets Pyre's own renderer draw
            it, so animations authored in Pyre reproduce exactly. Its silhouette
            and its paint are computed together in one pass (lighting, facet lines,
            glows, border), so there is no edge rule to hand the shape stage and
            no paint recipe to hand the fill stage. Splitting it would mean re-implementing
            every legacy Pyre form against the shape/fill contract; until that is
            done this stays monolithic.
